@meta
id: 19-02
title: Read the list
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: quickfix-nav
par: 51
minutes: 5
vscode: scroll the search results panel, click one
vimrc: set hidden
open: README.md

@brief
There are several `TODO` comments under `src/`, each tagged with a
ticket number. ORD-311 shipped last week, so its TODO is done and the
line goes. The other TODOs are still open and stay. You do not know
which file the ORD-311 comment is in, and you do not want to open each
hit to find out.

`:vimgrep` collects every hit into the quickfix list and jumps to the
first. `:copen` opens the list itself as a window across the bottom of
the screen, one hit per line: the file, the line and column, and the
text of the line. It is an ordinary vim window. `j` and `k` move in it,
`/` searches in it. Enter on a line jumps to that hit in the window
above. `:cclose` closes it again.

Find the ORD-311 comment by reading the list, jump to it, delete the
line, and finish. The other TODO lines must not change.

@keys
| `:copen` | open the quickfix window |
| `Enter` | in the quickfix window: jump to the hit under the cursor |
| `:cclose` | close the quickfix window |
| `:wqa` | write all, quit all, quickfix window included |

@hints
`:vimgrep /TODO/ **/*.ts` fills the list. Then `:copen` and read. The
text column shows the ticket number on each line.
--
Move onto the ORD-311 line, or search for it with `/311`, and press
Enter. The cursor is now on the comment in the file itself.
--
`dd` removes the line. The quickfix window is still open below you, so
`:wq` would close only the file window and leave vim running. `:wqa`
closes everything.

@solution
    :vimgrep /TODO/ **/*.ts<Enter>  :copen<Enter>  /311<Enter>  <Enter>  dd  :wqa<Enter>

Each line of the quickfix window reads `file|line col N| text`. The
text is what makes it a search results panel rather than a list of
coordinates: you read the hits, decide which matter, and go to those.
VS Code's panel does the same job and you would click. Here you press
Enter, and the window above changes to the file.

The quickfix window is a normal window in every way that matters.
`Ctrl-W w` moves between it and the file, `:q` inside it closes it,
and it counts as a window when you quit, which is why `:wq` from the
file leaves vim open with the list still showing. `:wqa` is the honest
ending whenever the list is open, or `:cclose` first and then `:wq`.

You could have typed `:cn` once instead of reading; the next lesson
covers that. Reading first is the habit to build, because the hit you
want is often not the next one, and because the list shows you things
you did not search for, like a second TODO with the same ticket.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  placedAt: Date;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    // TODO ORD-402: move the refund window check into the entity
    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).sendRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@start src/domain/order/order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
    };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    // TODO ORD-311: validate the id before calling the provider
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

